# Implementation Plan — SupplyGuard AI-Aware Supply Chain Security Scanner

Build SupplyGuard according to the 7-mission build plan in [SupplyGuard_Antigravity_Build_Plan.md](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/SupplyGuard_Antigravity_Build_Plan.md). SupplyGuard is an open-source, CLI + Flask dashboard security scanner that combines:
1. **SBOM Generation** via CycloneDX (`cyclonedx-py`)
2. **OSS Vulnerability Correlation** via OSV.dev batch API
3. **Secrets Detection** via Gitleaks with zero-leakage redaction
4. **Static Analysis (SAST)** with a custom 10-rule Semgrep pack targeting AI-generated code smells (CWE-mapped)
5. **Deterministic Risk Scoring Engine** persisting to SQLite via SQLAlchemy
6. **Dark-Mode Web Dashboard** powered by Flask, Jinja2, and Chart.js
7. **Vulnerable Demo Application & GitHub Actions CI Gate**

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Subprocess & Environment Tooling**:
> SupplyGuard invokes `cyclonedx-py`, `gitleaks`, and `semgrep` as external subprocesses (`shell=False`).
> - We will install Python packages (`cyclonedx-bom`, `click`, `flask`, `sqlalchemy`, `requests`, `pytest`, `rich`, `ruff`, etc.) in a dedicated `.venv`.
> - If `gitleaks` or `semgrep` binary is not found on the local system PATH at runtime, SupplyGuard will:
>   1. Provide clean, actionable error messages with direct download instructions.
>   2. Include robust mock suites in `tests/` and safe fallback handling so the core Python pipeline, scoring engine, CLI, and Web Dashboard are fully functional and verifiable.

