### Core Scanner Modules

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/\_\_init\_\_.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/__init__.py)
- Package initialization and version metadata.

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/models.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/models.py)
- SQLAlchemy models:
  - `Scan`: `id`, `project_path`, `started_at`, `finished_at`, `risk_score`, `components_count`, `findings_count`
  - `Finding`: `id`, `scan_id` (FK), `source` (`sbom_osv` / `secrets` / `sast`), `severity` (`CRITICAL` / `HIGH` / `MEDIUM` / `LOW` / `INFO`), `file`, `line`, `rule_id`, `cwe`, `message`, `raw_json`
- Database engine and session factory with SQLite default `supplyguard.db`.

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/sbom/generator.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/sbom/generator.py) (Mission 1)
- Typed dataclass `Component(name: str, version: str, purl: str = "")`
- `generate_sbom(project_path: Path, output_path: Path | None = None) -> tuple[Path, list[Component]]`
- Invokes `cyclonedx-py requirements` with `shell=False`, parses output CycloneDX JSON into components; handles missing requirements or tool gracefully.

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/vulns/osv_client.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/vulns/osv_client.py) (Mission 1)
- Typed dataclass `VulnMatch(package: str, version: str, vuln_id: str, severity: str, summary: str, fixed_version: str | None = None)`
- `batch_query(components: list[Component]) -> list[VulnMatch]`
- Batches components in chunks of up to 100 to `https://api.osv.dev/v1/querybatch`.
- Fetches detailed vulnerability data from `https://api.osv.dev/v1/vulns/{id}` with 10s timeout and 1 automatic retry on timeout.

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/secrets/scanner.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/secrets/scanner.py) (Mission 2)
- Typed dataclass `SecretFinding(file: str, line: int, rule_id: str, match_preview: str, description: str = "")`
- `scan_secrets(project_path: Path) -> list[SecretFinding]`
- Runs `gitleaks detect --source <path> --report-format json --report-path <temp_file> --no-git` via `subprocess.run(..., shell=False)`.
- **Zero-leak redaction**: Matches are strictly trimmed to first 3 + last 3 characters (`"AKIA..." -> "AKI...XYZ"`), never storing or logging raw secret values.

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/sast/rules/ai-code-smells.yml](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/sast/rules/ai-code-smells.yml) (Mission 3)
- 10 targeted Semgrep rules:
  1. `ai-sql-injection-concat`: String formatting/concatenation in SQL query (CWE-89)
  2. `ai-unprotected-admin-route`: Flask/FastAPI delete/update/admin route without auth decorator (CWE-862)
  3. `ai-unsafe-eval-exec-pickle`: `eval`, `exec`, `pickle.loads` on non-literal (CWE-94 / CWE-502)
  4. `ai-subprocess-shell-true`: `subprocess` with `shell=True` on non-literal (CWE-78)
  5. `ai-requests-verify-false`: HTTP request with `verify=False` (CWE-295)
  6. `ai-flask-debug-true`: Flask `app.run(debug=True)` in production/entrypoint (CWE-489)
  7. `ai-weak-hash-md5-sha1`: Weak hash algorithm used for credentials/security (CWE-916)
  8. `ai-jwt-unverified-decode`: `jwt.decode` with signature verification disabled or algorithm none (CWE-347)
  9. `ai-cors-wildcard-with-credentials`: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` with credentials enabled (CWE-942)
  10. `ai-insecure-random-token`: `random` module instead of `secrets` for tokens/passwords (CWE-330)

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/sast/scanner.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/sast/scanner.py) (Mission 3)
- Typed dataclass `SastFinding(file: str, line: int, rule_id: str, severity: str, cwe: str, message: str)`
- `run_sast(project_path: Path) -> list[SastFinding]`
- Invokes `semgrep` with `--config=supplyguard/sast/rules/ai-code-smells.yml` and `--json`. Includes internal pattern matching fallback if semgrep executable is absent.

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/scoring/engine.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/scoring/engine.py) (Mission 4)
- Deterministic weighted risk score calculation (`0-100`):
  - +10 per OSV CRITICAL, +5 per HIGH, +2 per MEDIUM/LOW
  - +15 per Secret finding (heaviest weight — immediately exploitable)
  - +8 per SAST HIGH finding, +3 per SAST MEDIUM finding, +1 per LOW
  - Capped at 100
- Computes source breakdowns and severity statistics.

#### [NEW] [supplyguard/cli.py](file:///c:/SupplyGaurd/supplyguard/cli.py) (Mission 4)
- Click CLI commands:
  - `supplyguard scan <path>`: Orchestrates SBOM generation -> OSV correlation, and parallel Secrets + SAST via `concurrent.futures`, executes scoring, persists to SQLite `supplyguard.db`, and outputs a rich terminal summary table.
  - `supplyguard report <scan_id>`: Displays detailed tabular breakdown of a previous scan.
  - `supplyguard web [--host] [--port]`: Starts the Flask dashboard server.

